But — hold on, one more important guard for the dev rule: the issue must not already carry a machine PR that the loop is handling. Consider an issue assigned to the machine whose dev leg ALREADY ran and produced PR #X (ai_developed label present → excluded via notLabels). ✓. Consider: dev leg ran, PR exists but is RED and review armed agent:rework on the ISSUE (rework-on-red-ci) → issue carries agent:rework → excluded ✓. Consider: dev leg produced PR, no ai_developed?? develop-done latches it when green. If the PR is open but red/none and NO agent:rework yet: issue carries no loop labels → dev-on-assignment would RE-dispatch a dev leg! Hmm — is that wrong? The dev leg already ran (PR exists). Re-dispatching dev = wasted leg + could duplicate... but wait — the rework-on-red-gate-unlatched rule (prMachineAuthor, red) arms rework; validate-fresh handles 'none'. The window: PR open + checks pending/none + no labels: validate-fresh dispatches validation... on the PR carrier (localAction validate_pr). Meanwhile dev-on-assignment would see the issue (assigned, no loop labels) and dispatch ANOTHER dev leg → duplicates!

Hmm. Guard needed: exclude issues that HAVE an open linked PR at all (any state): `query.prState`? There's `prState` guard — positive match only. I need "no open PR". Hmm — is there a `noPr`-style guard? Looking at matchesGuards: prState matches when `item.pr && item.pr.state === q.prState`. No "absent PR" guard. Options:
- Add a tiny guard `noOpenPr: true` in matchesGuards: `if (q.noOpenPr && item.pr && item.pr.state === 'OPEN') return false;` — hmm wait, also a merged/closed PR's issue: develop-done latches ai_developed... for a MERGED PR, close-on-merge closes the issue. An issue with a CLOSED machine PR (PR closed without merge — rare) and no labels: re-dev is CORRECT (the work died with the PR). So guard = exclude OPEN linked PR only. 

Let me check how enrichment populates item.pr for issues with a closed PR: line 545-551: `item.pr = {number, state: prRef.state, checks: 'none', mergeState: 'UNKNOWN'...}` — so state 'CLOSED'/'MERGED' visible. And prNumber set. So:

```js
if (q.noOpenPr) {
    if (item.pr && (item.pr.state === 'OPEN')) return false;
}
```

