### 1. Fix `scripts/restore-fa-session.sh`

Current:
```bash
  if git fetch --depth 1 origin "refs/heads/$FA_SESS_BRANCH"; then
    git checkout "refs/remotes/origin/$FA_SESS_BRANCH" -- .dmtools/fa-sessions
    # Unstage (checkout <ref> -- <path> STAGES): the session store
    # belongs on the fa-sess branch only.
    git restore --staged .dmtools/fa-sessions
    echo "→ fa session restored from $FA_SESS_BRANCH"
  else
    echo "→ no saved fa session yet ($FA_SESS_BRANCH absent) — starting fresh"
  fi
```

New:
```bash
  # gh-944: the fetch must carry a DESTINATION refspec. A bare
  # `refs/heads/<branch>` refspec materializes NO tracking ref in an
  # actions/checkout single-branch clone (remote.origin.fetch is pinned to
  # the head branch), so the checkout below either fails to resolve the ref
  # (rc 128) or hits a branch whose tree carries no store (the exact
  # "error: pathspec '.dmtools/fa-sessions' did not match any file(s)" that
  # killed both first-session dev legs on #925) — under `bash -e` either
  # shape kills the leg. `+` (force): persist force-pushes the branch.
  if git fetch --depth 1 origin "+refs/heads/$FA_SESS_BRANCH:refs/remotes/origin/$FA_SESS_BRANCH"; then
    # gh-944 acceptance (a): the checkout is a NO-OP when the branch exists
    # but carries no session store (first-session shape) — never a pathspec
    # error. ls-tree prints nothing for an absent path and stays safe inside
    # the [ -n ] guard even for an unresolvable ref.
